Subject: [PATCH] Finish model, firmware and full-SoC verification with real
 MNIST data

- cnn_fpga: shared hardware-matched model (padding=0, 169->10), retrained
  (FP32 92.42%), quantize.py with bit-exact integer model (int8 92.40%),
  exports weights and test vectors; fix broken extract_weights.py
- sw: 'W'/'S'/'B' UART protocol, cycle counts reported to the host,
  CPU-only baseline, no software division; Makefile emits .mif for Quartus
- sw/send_image.py: board run with real weights/digits, checks against Python
- tb/system: full-SoC test, 10 real digits, 100/100 logits bit-exact,
  830 accelerator cycles vs 3,928,305 CPU cycles
- cnn_soc_top.sdc; stop ignoring .qpf/.qsf; remove superseded dummy-weight TB

